## Permission-bit custody census — SPEC §3.2

The baseline is 0600 for the socket and 0700 for AX-owned directories. Each
cell runs the stated mode through the named production entry. Refusal cells
assert the literal error code and complete message and observe zero Dial,
Runner/spawn, or lifecycle dispatch. Ancestor read/execute cells are
`admitted-by-spec` under §3.2 lines 810–812: they do not grant write access
that could replace the socket. Sticky shared ancestors are separately driven
through all three entries by `TestCustodyPermissionBitCensusAdmitsStickyAncestor`.

